  it's professor perez hubby he's a  nuclear physicist and he also sat on the  un's advisory board on disarmament  matters a professor as an anti-nuclear  activist which you are what legacy do  you feel abdul khadija khan leaves  behind  well he  certainly initiated the uranium  enrichment program because he was  employed at urenko in belgium and there  he chanced upon those documents that he  was given to translate and so yes  i think that the uranium enrichment  program owes to him  however the actual fabrication of the  bomb the design and act and the testing  does not come from him it comes from the  pakistan atomic energy commission and  the  the  atomic energy commission and khan's  institute were at loggerheads they were  bitter rivals as far as his being a  scientist he's always  advertised in the news as a nuclear  scientist he was not  he was a metallurgist and  i think his greatest contribution was uh  perhaps in  in reverse engineering  i also i think that uh what you have  just played  doesn't convey the fact that he died a  very bitter man and he  thought that  he had been robbed of his legacy  that the army  who had  in fact recruited him and  under and which worked essentially under  him betrayed him  in  the matter of professor  because we briefly interrupted here  because you talked about his legacy many  analysts say that nuclear deterrence  between india and pakistan worked in  preventing them from going to war with  each other  was he responsible for for that at least  in part  no i don't think he had anything to do  with policy the fact that pakistan has  nuclear weapons  of course prevents  india and pakistan from going to war  against each other however  very interestingly it was nuclear  weapons that initiated the cargill  conflict and this was one in which about  three to four thousand people died on  both sides and this is a war that would  not have occurred but for the existence  of nuclear weapons because pakistan felt  itself sufficiently secure  and so it felt that it could  it could uh send  troops disguised of course across the  international border across the line of  control and that's what caused the  conflict so it's i think a very unique  case of nuclear weapons actually causing  a war  professor purvis hood boy physicist and  antinuclear activist thank you very much  you
 

